  "notes": [
    "Community list transcribed from the 'Napoleonic Wargames' Ottoman Empire Black Powder supplement (see attribution/source link). Unit combat stats (Hand-to-Hand, Shooting, Morale, Stamina) and armament have not yet been entered — only costs and force organisation from the points chart are included so far. Check the source for full unit profiles before playing.",
    "This builder omits several of the book's point-modifier upgrades/downgrades — apply these manually per the book: any Janissary, Guard Janissary, Sekhan, Kapikulu, Sipahi, Deli or Nizam-i-Cedid unit may be upgraded to Large (+8 pts/unit) or downgraded to Small (-8 pts/unit); any unit or regiment may be downgraded to Wavering (-8 pts/unit, -4 if Small, -12 if Large); Divisional and Positional Artillery batteries may be upgraded to Large (+8 or +12 pts/battery) or downgraded to a Half Battery (-8 or -12 pts/battery).",
    "Baktasi and other add-ons (not modelled as selectable options): any Janissary or Guard Janissary unit may take a Baktasi for +6 pts (+9 if Large); Nizam-i-Cedid units may be 'Freshly Raised' for +2 pts (+1 if Small, +4 if Large).",
    "Only one commander in the whole army may have Strategy/Staff Rating 8."
  ],
  "specialRules": [
    "The C-in-C may be the Sultan himself (+25 pts on top of Staff Rating), giving all commanders +1 to their C-in-C re-rolls. Taking the Sultan unlocks Kapikulu Guard Cavalry Brigades, lets the Guard Janissary Brigade take Solaks, and allows one Mameluke-only Deli Brigade."
  ]
}
